Subject: [PATCH 5/5] rusticc: timelapse, moonraker-timelapse ported to Rust

A built-in timelapse component with moonraker-timelapse c7fff11's API and
behaviour (component/timelapse.py): the /machine/timelapse/* endpoints,
the timelapse_newframe/_saveFrames/_render remote methods its Klipper
macros call, the timelapse:timelapse_event notification, the settings in
the 'timelapse' database namespace with moonraker.conf overrides
(blockedsettings), frames by wget from the webcam's snapshot URL, render
by ffmpeg/libx264. Built in, so Mainsail's timelapse tab works without
loading Python (the Python component costs ~9 MB on the CC1). A built-in
name wins over a timelapse.py in the Moonraker tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
